hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"945","978 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Shuba informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Every boy is pledged for his aqiqa; it is slaughtered for him on the seventh day, his head is shaved, and he is named."
"946","979 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Umar al-Qasabi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed aqiqa for al-Hasan and al-Husayn, a ram each."
"947","980 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Mamar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed aqiqa for al-Hasan with a ram and for al-Husayn with a ram. 981 - al-Thawri, Ibn Uyayna, Hammad ibn Zayd and others narrated it from Ayyub, not going beyond Ikrima with it."
"948","982 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said, from Abu Hurayra, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No fara and no atira."
